        "trackId": "ks-12-4516-municipal",
        "affectedElement": "filing_process",
        "question": "The municipal filing fee. K.S.A. 12-4516(g)(2) lets a municipal court prescribe a fee to be charged as costs, and the amount varies court by court with no statewide figure. No figure may be quoted until the participant's court is known."
      },
      {
        "trackId": "ks-12-4516-municipal",
        "affectedElement": "correct_form",
        "question": "Which Kansas municipal courts publish their own current expungement forms or require their own process, and which govern expungement by charter ordinance rather than by K.S.A. 12-4516 directly. Kansas has hundreds of municipal courts and no unified municipal forms regime; a bounded sample confirmed that Wichita proceeds under Charter Ordinance No. 224 and publishes a Motion and Order, while Topeka publishes its own petition and order forms under K.S.A. 12-4516. The statewide controlled pleading is the fallback only where the local court publishes nothing."
      },
      {
